105:/// A transfer's SOURCE path for the wire (cr-uv2-1):
106:/// [`relative_path_to_posix`], with a `/` after it when the path was typed
107:/// as a directory. The end that holds the source then knows what was
108:/// asked for — `single.txt/` is a directory or it is nothing, as it is to
109:/// `cp`, `mv` and `rsync` — where it was told `single.txt` and copied the
110:/// file. The module's root needs no mark.
111:pub fn source_path_to_posix(path: &Path) -> String {
112:    let mut posix = relative_path_to_posix(path);
113:    if !posix.is_empty() && posix != "." && typed_as_directory(path) {
114:        posix.push('/');
115:    }
116:    posix
117:}
