96:/// Resolve a destination file path as `base.join(rel)`, but preserving
97:/// `base` verbatim when `rel` is empty. `PathBuf::join("")` appends a
98:/// trailing separator on Unix (e.g. `/a/b` + `""` → `/a/b/`), which
99:/// `File::create` then rejects with `ENOTDIR` when `base` is itself
100:/// the intended file path (single-file push flow).
101:pub(crate) fn resolve_dest_path(base: &Path, rel: &Path) -> PathBuf {
102:    if rel.as_os_str().is_empty() {
103:        base.to_path_buf()
104:    } else {
105:        base.join(rel)
106:    }
107:}
