109:/// Join `rel` under `module.path` and verify the resolved location
110:/// stays inside the module's canonical root after symlink expansion.
111:/// Closes F2 of `docs/reviews/codebase_review_2026-05-01.md`.
112:///
113:/// Containment is checked against `module.canonical_root`, not
114:/// `module.path`. The push handler may rewrite `module.path` to
115:/// include a destination subpath (rsync "copy into here" semantics),
116:/// so `module.path` isn't reliably the canonical root anymore.
117:/// `module.canonical_root` is set once at runtime load time and
118:/// never mutated.
